{
  "result": "I'd decouple survival from usefulness.\n\nNo one would have to earn the right to be fed, housed, rested, cared for when they're sick, or treated with dignity when they're old, disabled, grieving, failing, or just not productive in a way anyone can measure.\n\nSo much cruelty doesn't come from people genuinely being monsters. It comes from fear \u2014 fear that if you stop, slow down, need too much, or become inconvenient, you'll fall through the floor and no one will catch you. People hoard, compete, stay silent, harden themselves, because they believe there's only enough safety for the valuable.\n\nIf that floor was just... there. Unconditional. I think people would be braver, and kinder, in a way no moral lecture could make them.\n\nThat's the one change I'd make.",
